8:["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","main",null,{"id":"main-content","className":"min-h-screen bg-bg pt-24","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Article\",\"headline\":\"Fix Mobile CTA Position to Boost Mobile Ad Conversions\",\"description\":\"Your CTA looks fine on your flagship phone - but on 375px screens it disappears below the fold before visitors ever scroll. Here's the layout problem, and how to fix it.\",\"author\":{\"@id\":\"https://nebulacomponents.com/#founder\"},\"datePublished\":\"2026-07-25\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-07-25\",\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https://nebulacomponents.com/#organization\"},\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://nebulacomponents.com/learning-centre/cta-below-fold-mobile\"},\"image\":\"https://nebulacomponents.com/opengraph-image\"}"}}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-14","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-8 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8 md:p-10","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-accent uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-sm font-semibold mb-4","children":"Mobile Leaks"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-fg leading-tight mb-6","children":"Fix Mobile CTA Position to Boost Mobile Ad Conversions"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-lg leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"You tested it on your phone. It looked fine. You shipped it. But your phone is a recent flagship with a tall screen and plenty of viewport real estate. On an iPhone SE or a budget Android - the devices that make up a significant slice of real-world traffic - your primary CTA is invisible until the visitor scrolls. Most of them never do. This is the mobile blind spot that quietly hurts conversion rates that have already been \"optimised.\""}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-stretch sm:items-center gap-3","children":[["$","$L19",null,{"href":"/audit?utm_source=learning-centre-cta-below-fold-mobile&utm_medium=hero-cta","className":"inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center justify-center rounded bg-accent px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-bg transition-opacity hover:opacity-85","children":"Get your free audit →"}],["$","$L19",null,{"href":"/repair-sprint","className":"inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center justify-center rounded border border-border px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-fg-muted transition-colors hover:border-fg-muted hover:text-fg","children":"Explore $97 Repair Sprint"}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-fg mb-4","children":"The Device Blind Spot Founders Never Catch"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted mb-4","children":"When founders say they've \"checked mobile,\" they almost always mean they opened their site on their own device. That device is typically a recent iPhone Pro or a current-generation Android flagship - a screen that is taller, sharper, and more forgiving than what a meaningful portion of their audience is actually using."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted mb-4","children":"The result is a form of survivorship bias baked into the QA process. The founder sees the CTA. The tester sees the CTA. The designer sees the CTA. But the visitor on a 375px-wide screen with a 667px viewport height sees a hero section, a navigation bar, and a lot of padding - and then bounces before they ever reach the button that was supposed to convert them."}],"$L1a"]}],"$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21"]}]]}],null,"$L22"]}]
